        "original_id": "2332ad14-93c3-50ce-ab8a-6bef7642833c",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Leonard Stogel, Sam the Sham, Domingo \"Sam\" Samudio\n- Musical Groups: Sweathog, The Cowsills, Tommy James & The Shondells, Redbone, Gentle Giant, Napoleon XIV, The Royal Guardsmen\n- Places: Dallas, Texas\n- Roles: music manager, rock and roll singer\n- Topics: stage persona, performance image\n\nFacts:\n- Domingo \"Sam\" Samudio was born on 28 February 1937 in Dallas, Texas.\n- Domingo \"Sam\" Samudio is better known by the stage name Sam the Sham.\n- Sam the Sham is a retired American rock and roll singer.\n- Sam the Sham was known for wearing a camp robe and turban.\n- Sam the Sham hauled his equipment in a 1952 Packard hearse with maroon velvet curtains.\n- Leonard Stogel managed Sam the Sham and musical groups including Sweathog, The Cowsills, Tommy James & The Shondells, Redbone, Gentle Giant, Napoleon XIV, and The Royal Guardsmen.",
